    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1">

                <pb facs="0035" n="1" sameAs="frus:frus1897/pg1"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Olney to Mr.
                            Buchanan.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-12-31"><hi rendition="#italic">December 31,
                        1896</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 187.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose a copy of a letter<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d1-f1"/> from Mr. E. F. Skinner alleging a discrimination by the
                    Argentine Government against American and in favor of Canadian lumber.</p>
                <p>It is presumed that, if it exists, it is in virtue of a special reciprocity
                    treaty.</p>
                <p>The Department would be glad to be advised on the subject.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Richard Olney.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
